Keep a shared target as empty text.
Keep a shared stickers as an empty list of text.
Keep a shared letters as an empty list of text.
Keep a shared bits as an empty list of whole numbers.
Keep a shared costs as an empty list of whole numbers.
Keep a shared currentsticker as empty text.
Keep a shared letter as empty text.
Keep a shared nextmask as 0.
Keep a shared matchpos as 0.
Place "thehat" into target.
Place "with" into stickers.
Place "example" into stickers.
Place "science" into stickers.
For every spot from 0 to the last position of target.
The piece is the slice of target from spot to spot plus 1.
Place piece into letters.

Place 1 into bits.
For every step from 1 to 6.
The ending is the last position of bits.
The prior is item ending of bits.
The doubled is prior times 2.
Place doubled into bits.

For every spot from 0 to 63.
Place 999 into costs.

Set item 0 of costs to 0.

To find from spot (a whole number).
If matchpos is at least 0, return.
If spot is more than the last position of letters, return.
The raised is item spot of bits.
The bit is bitwise and of nextmask and raised.
If bit is not 0, find from spot plus 1, return.
If item spot of letters matches letter, set matchpos to spot, return.
Find from spot plus 1.

To paste from marker (a whole number).
The final is the last position of currentsticker.
For every spot from 0 to final.
Set letter to the slice of currentsticker from spot to spot plus 1.
Set matchpos to -1.
Find from 0.
The slot is matchpos.
If slot is at least 0, set nextmask to nextmask plus item slot of bits.

To apply from mask (a whole number).
For every index from 0 to the last position of stickers.
Set currentsticker to item index of stickers.
Set nextmask to mask.
Paste from index.
The start is mask.
The candidate is item start of costs plus 1.
The slot is nextmask.
If item slot of costs is more than candidate, set item slot of costs to candidate.

For every mask from 0 to 63.
If item mask of costs is less than 999, apply from mask.

Show item 63 of costs.
